            <ArticleTitle>Clinical and surgical aspects of posterior fossa haemangioblastomata.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retrospective study has been carried out on 67 patients with posterior fossa haemangioblastomata. Clinical details are presented, and the problems of diagnosis discussed. A fresh definition of the von Hippel-Lindau complex is put forward. The results of surgery are good for patients with solitary and sporadic tumours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
